<title>FRANCE: GEC ALSTHOM WINS SINGAPORE METRO LINE CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>GEC ALSTHOM WINS SINGAPORE METRO LINE CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-British group GEC Alsthom said on Monday it had won a contract worth 500 million francs in alliance with ST Electronic and Engineering to equip a new metro underground railway line covering 20 km and 16 stations.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the contract for the North East Line had been awarded by the Land Transport Authority to it and its Singapore partner.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
